Petey chatted with the newly crowned  pageant queen exclusively on Friday  about her groundbreaking win for the  LGBT community I'm on cloud nine I'm  ready to go to Miss America and I'm  really happy to have made history I am  definitely the first openly gay Miss  Missouri and the first woman to go into  the Miss America competition openly gay  Aaron O'Flaherty took home the title of  Miss Missouri Saturday after winning  overall in all areas of competition the  23 year old beauty queen plans to spend  her reign promoting a cause that hits  close to home  when I was 13 I lost one of my best  friends to suicide and it was through  the grieving process that I realized  that there were warning signs and maybe  this could have been prevented  so I'm now an advocate for the American  Foundation for Suicide Prevention Aaron  came out at 18 and it looks like she's  now a trailblazer for lesbian women in  the pageant system in the past few days  I've received several messages from  other contestants that are out in other  states so that's awesome to hear that  maybe I won't even be the only one going  to Miss America this year openly lesbian  so that is really exciting I saw most of  my success after I came out because I  was able to present myself as exactly  who I am  watch Erin compete for Miss America on  September 11th in Atlantic City New  Jersey  you
 

